 ## Overview
-SDF Primitives are analytical Signed Distance Functions that compute the exact Euclidean distance from a query point in 3D space to the surface of a basic geometric shape, returning a negative value if the point is inside and a positive value if it is outside [S1, S3, S5, S7, S8, unofficial]. They serve as the foundational building blocks for distance-field ray marching, enabling efficient step-size estimation by guaranteeing that the returned distance is never an underestimation, which prevents ray overshooting [S1, S7, unofficial]. Unlike [SDF Domain Manipulation Operators](1730-sdf-domain-manipulation-operators.md) which transform space, or [SDF Rounding](1829-sdf-rounding.md) which modifies surfaces, primitives define the base geometry itself [S7, unofficial].
