 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per primitive evaluation. Most primitives involve a constant number of arithmetic operations and square roots [S1, S3, S5, S7, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$, requiring only the query point and primitive parameters [S7, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Exact and efficient, free of numerical noise for standard primitives [S7, unofficial]. The Rhombic Triacontahedron is more expensive due to multiple folds and trigonometric constants, but still $O(1)$ [S8, unofficial].
